{"tuid":"uv7zle9662t1n69l","pageVersion":12,"fetchedAt":"2026-09-30T09:55:56.751Z","record":{"colophon":{"generator":"ifdb.org/viewgame","generatorversion":1,"originated":"2024-02-23"},"identification":{"ifids":["B65AE81F-9457-4793-973C-08871EED13CD"],"format":"glulx"},"bibliographic":{"title":"To Sea in a Sieve","author":"J. J. Guest","language":"en","firstpublished":"2023-10-01","genre":"Comedy, pyratical yarn","description":"Peter Petibon, cabin boy, hath a problem. He be goin&#039; down -- to Davy Jones&#039; locker, by the powers! Lest he seize the booty o&#039; the dread pyrate Booby, and heave it all o&#039;erboard, he and the Cap&#039;n both will be hors d&#039;oeuvres for the sharks. But what be in that mysterious sea-chest? Do beavers eat boats? And what, i&#039; the devil&#039;s name be THE DREADED &quot;YATEVEO&quot; TREE? All o&#039; these questions, an&#039; more besides, will be answered when ye play &quot;To Sea in a Sieve&quot;, a one-room game by J. J. Guest. \n<p> \nTo Sea in a Sieve is a prequel to the author&#039;s 2003 game  \n<a href=\"viewgame?id=6d9dfn2akcrlq1bu\">To Hell in a Hamper</a>. Set 160 years earlier, To Sea in a Sieve will eventually form the first part of a trilogy. No knowledge of To Hell in a Hamper is needed to enjoy To Sea in a Sieve."},"contacts":[],"ifdb":{"tuid":"uv7zle9662t1n69l","pageversion":12,"link":"https://ifdb.org/viewgame?id=uv7zle9662t1n69l","coverart":{"url":"https://ifdb.org/coverart?id=uv7zle9662t1n69l&version=12"},"playTimeInMinutes":35,"primaryPlayOnlineUrl":"https://iplayif.com/?story=https%3A%2F%2Funbox.ifarchive.org%2F%3Furl%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Fifarchive.org%252Fif-archive%252Fgames%252Fcompetition2023%252FGames%252FTo%252520Sea%252520in%252520a%252520Sieve.zip%26open%3DTo%2BSea%2Bin%2Ba%2BSieve%252FTo%2BSea%2Bin%2Ba%2BSieve.gblorb","downloads":{"links":[{"url":"https://ifarchive.org/if-archive/games/competition2023/Games/To%20Sea%20in%20a%20Sieve.zip","playOnlineUrl":"https://iplayif.com/?story=https%3